    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d648">

                <pb facs="0798" n="674" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg674"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.00/1972: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Representative on Special Mission in Cuba</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Crowder</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-01-27T08:00:00-05:29"><hi rendition="#italic">January 27,
                                1921—8 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 6:05 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>At conference yesterday referred to in my urgent 14, January 26, 6 p.m.,<anchor
                        n="11" xml:id="d648-f1"/> I made very explicit statement that if, through
                    failure of courts to act promptly on contested election cases, the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ad interim</hi>
                    <pb facs="0799" n="675" xml:id="pg675"/> administration of municipalities should
                    continue, followed by <hi rendition="#italic">ad interim</hi> administration of
                    provinces commencing on February 24th, and <hi rendition="#italic">ad
                        interim</hi> administration of the nation on and after May 21st, with total
                    paralysis of legislative power on first Monday in April 1921,<anchor n="12"
                        xml:id="d648-f2"/> a similar statement would be presented under Platt
                    Amendment of change of Ministers to maintain a Government adequate for
                    protection of life and property and individual liberty making it very difficult
                    if not impossible to avoid actual intervention. Statement was received without
                    the slightest offense. I think effect will be greatly to stimulate action by
                    courts and also action by Congress on amendments to the electoral code necessary
                    to expedite partial elections which in all probability must be held.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Crowder</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
